Uses / definitions: B1 defines i, j, a; B2 uses and defines i, j; B3 defines a; B4 uses a and defines i. B4 goes to B2 or exit.

- $IN(B2)=\{i,j\}\cup(OUT(B2)-\{i,j\})$

- $IN(B4)=\{a\}\cup(OUT(B4)-\{i\})$, $IN(B3)=OUT(B3)-\{a\}$

Iterating to a fixed point:

- OUT(B4) = IN(B2) = {a, i, j}

- IN(B4) = {a, j} = OUT(B3); IN(B3) = {j}

- OUT(B2) = IN(B3) $\cup$ IN(B4) = {a, j}

- OUT(B1) = IN(B2) = {a, i, j}
